      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "infra. समाप्ति = पूर्णता, नाश. Râmarshi, who adds यामन्नवसनशयन-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "वासादिवृत्तिं प्राप्तुमितस्ततो नीचस्थलेष्वप्युद्यच्छमानानां न कश्चिदपि गुणस्तिष्ठतीत्यर्थः—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "The word समाप्ति occurs at Naishadha III., 118 where too the com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "mentator renders it by संपूर्णता. The meaning is that there is no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "scope for the exercise of one's merits, all the energies being",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "absorbed in the ‘ struggle for existence.’ The Stanza occurs also",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "at p. 302 of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XI.—The distinction between स्वर्ग and संसारविच्छित्ति is note-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "worthy. Comp. the note to St. III., supra स्वर्गद्वारकपाटपाटन. Comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Mahânâṭaka p. 148..—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XII.—भुक्ताः = preyed upon (i. e. by the desire for the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "enjoyments or भोगाः which we have not enjoyed). Râmarshi says",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "विटिकरणेन (?) पामरजनैः पराभूताः. The other commentary agrees",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with our interpretation याताः = गतसत्त्वा Râmarshi. The other com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "mentator says यस्मिन्काले यत्कर्म कर्तुमुचितं तत्कर्मविहीनो यातो गतः (sic °हीना",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "याता गताः ?) It appears to mean as good as gone out of the world",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "comp. Gîtâ I., 9. जीर्णा – comp. St. II. जीर्णाः = enfeebled by old",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "age.—Upajâti.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XIII.—The commentary on this is very involved and un-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "intelligible. It runs this गृहे यदुचितं भोजनादिसुखं तत्क्षमया न क्षान्तं किं तु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "रोगादिपरवशेन संतोषादलंवुद्ध्या त्यक्तमपि न शीतादयः सोढाः तपनोग्निः दारिद्र्यभावेन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "क्लेशान् शास्त्रीयं तु तपः यच्चान्द्रादिरूपं तु न तप्तं तत्तत्कर्म तादृशं तादृशं कर्म कृतं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "तत्तत्फलैः तेषां तेषां कर्मणां फलैर्मुनिभिः कर्मोपदेष्टृभिः तर्जत् एव निश्चितं वञ्चितं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "लध्वीकृतमित्यर्थः. The first line may be translated as follows: “We",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "pardoned [injuries] but not through forgiveness; we abandoned",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "the pleasures suited to a home, but not through contentedness.”;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "the idea being that the former was the result of inability",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "to revenge and the latter of inability to get the plea-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "sures in question, in neither case was there the exercise of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "self-abnegation. In the second line °न क्लेशा न is a better reading",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
